# Mandatory Phased Delivery Rule

- Read `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` before planning or changing this repository.
- Treat that document as the controlling scope, sequence, test plan, and definition of done.
- Work only on the current authorized phase in its Progress Register.
- Do not begin, partially implement, or bundle work from a later phase.
- Preserve existing user changes and inspect the working tree before editing.
- Never reset, discard, or rewrite unrelated work to make a phase pass.
- Add unit tests for changed business logic and regression tests for fixed defects.
- Run every automated check required by the current phase.
- Do not weaken, delete, skip, or mark a test flaky merely to obtain a passing result.
- After automated tests pass, provide the owner with the phase's manual checklist.
- A phase remains incomplete until the owner explicitly confirms manual acceptance.
- Update the Progress Register only after evidence is recorded and the owner approves.
- Do not move to the next phase without explicit owner approval.
- If blocked, stop and report the exact blocker; do not expand scope silently.
- Emergency work outside the current phase requires explicit owner authorization and must be recorded in the plan.
- At phase completion, provide the report defined in the plan, including commands, results, defects, risks, and approval status.
